-- CONTROL for #1376.  Byte-identical to main.mdk except that the first import adds the
-- TYPE member: `import armod.{Cfg, mkA}` instead of `import armod.{mkA}`.
--
-- That ONE member is what both existing remedies key on (A-2.6's `memberOverlayDecl` and
-- #1319 unit 2's `applyRecordScopeOverrides`), so this spelling runs clean at `7`.
--
-- It is also what proves this is NOT #1283: #1283 is defined by the RE-EXPORT hop —
-- naming the re-exporter fails where naming the DECLARING module succeeds.  Here there is
-- no re-exporter at all and `armod` is named directly in BOTH files; the only variable is
-- whether the type is a member.
import armod.{Cfg, mkA}
import zrmod.{zrf}

main : <IO> Unit
main = println (mkA.fld + zrf 0)
